'en','Document Type',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5151,'resource_document_title_file','en','File',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5155,'resource_document_title_title_key','en','Title',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5156,'resource_document_title_user_id','en','User',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5158,'resource_document_type_contact_group_title_contact_group','en','Contact Group',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5159,'resource_document_type_contact_group_title_document_type_id','en','Document Type',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5160,'resource_document_type_title_contact_groups','en','Contact Groups',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5161,'resource_document_type_title_document_category','en','Category',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5162,'resource_document_type_title_name','en','Name',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5163,'resource_documentation_1034','en','Sure, here\'s the documentation for the `send-mail` component:\n\n**Description:**\nThe `send-mail` component is a PHP library function that allows you to send emails to a specified recipient. It checks if the recipient is unsubscribed from the mailing list before sending the email. The function also includes an unsubscribe link in the email header, making it easy for the recipient to opt-out of future emails.\n\n**Usage:**\nTo use the `send-mail` component, you can call the `sendMail()` function and pass in the following parameters:\n\n- `$receiver`: The email address of the recipient.\n- `$subject`: The subject line of the email.\n- `$text`: The body of the email.\n- `$type` (optional): The type of email being sent (e.g., \"all_mail\").\n\nHere\'s an example of how to use the `send-mail` component:\n\n```php\nsendMail(\'recipient@example.com\', \'Important Update\', \'This is the email body text.\');\n```\n\nIn this example, the `sendMail()` function is called with the recipient\'s email address, the subject line, and the email body text. The `$type` parameter is not provided, so the default value of \"all_mail\" will be used.\n\n**When to Use:**\nThe `send-mail` component should be used whenever you need to send an email to a recipient. It is particularly useful when you need to manage a mailing list and ensure that unsubscribed recipients do not receive emails. The inclusion of the unsubscribe link in the email header makes it easy for recipients to opt-out of future emails.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5164,'resource_documentation_1043','en','Sure, here\'s a short description of the provided PHP component and how it can be used:\n\nThis PHP component provides a set of utility functions for synchronizing resources and translations in a web application. The main functions are:\n\n1. `saveScriptsForResource($resourceName)`: This function saves the scripts for a given resource name. It checks the server configuration (WordPress or not) and then either includes a script file or makes a remote call to save the scripts.\n\n2. `getResourceDependencies($resourcename, $database)`: This function retrieves the dependencies for a given resource name from the database. It recursively fetches the dependencies and returns an array of all the dependencies.\n\n3. `getLanguagesCommaseparated($db)`: This function retrieves all the language keys from the database and returns them as a comma-separated string.\n\n4. `syncTranslations($repositoryURL, $serverDB, $resourcename)`: This function synchronizes the translations for a given resource name. It fetches the remote translations from the repository URL and updates the local translations in the server database.\n\n5. `getAllTranslationKeys($db,$resourceName)`: This function retrieves all the translation keys for a given resource name. It extracts the keys from the resource\'s title, documentation, parameters, and implementation.\n\nThese functions can be used in a web application that needs to manage resources and translations. For example, you can call `saveScriptsForResource()` whenever a resource is updated, `getResourceDependencies()` to ensure all dependencies are installed, and `syncTranslations()` to keep the translations up-to-date.\n\nHere\'s an example of how you might use the `saveScriptsForResource()` function:\n\n```php\n<?php\n$resourceName = \'my-resource\';\nsaveScriptsForResource($resourceName);\n?>\n```',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5165,'resource_documentation_1098','en','The `<object.viewparameter>` component is a custom tag that is used to display a parameter value within an object view. It is designed to be used in conjunction with the `Resource` class, which provides information about the parameter type.\n\nThe component has the following features:\n\n1. **Parameter Display**: The component displays the value of a parameter, along with an optional label. The label can be translated using the `translate()` function.\n\n2. **Parameter Type**: The component uses the `Resource` class to determine the type of the parameter, and then selects the appropriate viewer component to display the value.\n\n3. **Documentation**: If the parameter has a `documentation` attribute, the component will display it in a separate paragraph.\n\nTo use the `<object.viewparameter>` component, you would include it in your HTML template and pass in the necessary parameters:\n\n```html\n<object.viewparameter parameter=\"{{ myParameter }}\" value=\"{{ myValue }}\"></object.viewparameter>\n```\n\nIn this example, `myParameter` is an object that represents the parameter, and `myValue` is the value of the parameter.\n\nThe component will then use the information in the `myParameter` object to determine the appropriate viewer component to use, and will display the value of the parameter along with any additional information, such as a label or documentation.\n\nOverall, the `<object.viewparameter>` component is a useful tool for displaying parameter values within an object view, and can be used in a variety of contexts where you need to display dynamic data.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5166,'resource_documentation_1122','en','The `resource_dropdown_filter` component is a dropdown filter that allows users to search and select options from a list. It should be used when you need to provide a dropdown filter functionality in your application, such as for filtering data or selecting values from a list.\n\nHere\'s an example of how to use the `resource_dropdown_filter` component:\n\n```html\n<my-component-name label=\"Filter by\" name=\"filter\" datasource=\"my_resource\"></my-component-name>\n```\n\nIn this example, the `resource_dropdown_filter` component is used with the following parameters:\n\n- `label`: The label for the dropdown filter.\n- `name`: The name of the form field.\n- `datasource`: The resource that provides the options for the dropdown filter.\n\nThe component will render a dropdown filter with a search input, and the options will be loaded from the specified datasource. Users can type in the search input to filter the options, and select an option by clicking on it.\n\nThe component also supports additional features, such as:\n\n- Displaying a default \"Please select\" option.\n- Sorting the options alphabetically.\n- Handling keyboard navigation (up/down arrows, Enter, Escape, Tab).\n- Providing a callback function for when an option is clicked.\n\nOverall, the `resource_dropdown_filter` component is a useful tool for adding a flexible and customizable dropdown filter to your application.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5168,'resource_documentation_1162','en','Sure, here\'s a short description of the Toast component and how to use it:\n\nThe Toast component is a reusable UI element that displays temporary notifications or messages to the user. It is typically used to provide feedback or alerts to the user, such as successful form submissions, error messages, or other important information.\n\nThe Toast component should be used when you need to display a temporary message to the user that does not require immediate user interaction. It is designed to be unobtrusive and automatically disappear after a short period of time, unless the message requires user confirmation.\n\nTo use the Toast component, you can add the following HTML tag to your template:\n\n```html\n<my-component-name param_1=\"abc\"></my-component-name>\n```\n\nThe `param_1` attribute can be used to pass any necessary parameters to the Toast component, such as the message to display, whether the message requires confirmation, and the CSS class to apply to the message.\n\nFor example, to display a success message with a custom CSS class, you could use the following code:\n\n```html\n<my-component-name message=\"Your form was submitted successfully!\" type=\"success\" css-class=\"custom-toast\"></my-component-name>\n```\n\nThe Toast component will then display the message in a toast notification, with the specified CSS class applied to the message. The message will automatically disappear after a short period of time, unless the message requires user confirmation.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5169,'resource_documentation_1201','en','The Translate Tag is a custom HTML tag that allows you to easily translate text on your web page. It is designed to work with a translation system that stores translations in a database and provides a way to retrieve them.\n\nHere\'s how you can use the Translate Tag:\n\n```html\n<translate key=\"my_translation_key\" parameters=\'{\"param1\": \"value1\", \"param2\": \"value2\"}\'></translate>\n```\n\nThe `key` attribute specifies the translation key that should be used to look up the translation in the database. The `parameters` attribute is an optional JSON object that can be used to provide any dynamic parameters that the translation might need.\n\nThe Translate Tag component uses a global `translate()` function to handle the translation process. This function looks up the translation in the database based on the provided key, and then applies any necessary parameter substitutions.\n\nThe Translate Tag component should be used whenever you need to display translated text on your web page. It provides a simple and consistent way to manage translations, and helps to keep your HTML code clean and maintainable.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5170,'resource_documentation_895','en','Sure, here\'s the documentation for the `slugify` component:\n\nThe `slugify` component is a PHP library that provides two functions:\n\n1. `slugify($title)`: This function takes a string `$title` as input and returns a \"slugified\" version of the title. The slugified version is a string that is suitable for use in URLs or other contexts where a human-readable, URL-friendly version of a title is needed. The function performs the following transformations:\n   - Replaces any non-word characters (such as spaces, punctuation, etc.) with a hyphen.\n   - Removes any leading or trailing hyphens.\n   - Replaces multiple consecutive hyphens with a single hyphen.\n   - Converts the entire string to lowercase.\n\n2. `slugifyUnique($title, $table, $column, $db)`: This function takes a string `$title`, the name of a database table `$table`, the name of a column in that table `$column`, and a database connection object `$db` as input. It first calls the `slugify()` function to get the initial slugified version of the title. It then checks if that slug already exists in the specified table and column. If it does, the function appends a number to the end of the slug and increments the number until a unique slug is found. This function is useful when you need to ensure that each slugified title is unique within a database.\n\nHere\'s an example of how you might use the `slugify` component:\n\n```php\n$title = \"My Awesome Blog Post\";\n$slug = slugify($title); // Output: \"my-awesome-blog-post\"\n\n$uniqueSlug = slugifyUnique($title, \"blog_posts\", \"slug\", $db);\n// Output: \"my-awesome-blog-post\" (or \"my-awesome-blog-post-2\", \"my-awesome-blog-post-3\", etc. if the slug is not unique)\n```\n\nThe `slugify` component is useful whenever you need to generate a URL-friendly version of a title or other string. This is common in web applications, where you might want to use the slugified title in the URL for a blog post, product page, or other content. The `slugifyUnique` function is particularly useful when you need to ensure that each slugified title is unique within a database, such as when creating new blog posts or other content items.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5171,'resource_documentation_app','en','The main app component!',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5173,'resource_documentation_change','en','Will be fired when the text in the textarea changed. The event variable contains the text from this textarea.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5176,'resource_documentation_current_document_number','en','The current count of the document, e.g. you can start with bill number 1000, etc. if already in use, please do not change.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5177,'resource_documentation_database_table_editor','en','For your web application, manually managing numerous database tables through platforms like phpMyAdmin or by creating individual interfaces for each table can be quite cumbersome. Our system simplifies this process by automatically creating a table editor for you.\n\nThis intuitive editor offers a comprehensive overview of all the rows in a database table, facilitating effortless search, viewing, and modification of data.\n\n- *Sorting Function* Click on the column name to sort (A-Z). A second click sorts in reverse order (Z-A).\n- *Edit* Records can be edited with a click on the edit icon.\n- *Delete* Records can be deleted with a click on the trash bin icon.\n- *Appropriate Form Components like Dropdown, Radio Buttons, Number Input Fields* Utilizing the form generator (form.resource), it creates fitting form components based on defined parameters.\n- *Linked Tables with Dropdown* For instance, the system will conveniently display the corresponding country name in a dropdown menu when a user is associated with a \'country_id\', enhancing user-friendliness.\n- *Search Function Searches Linked Records* The advanced search functionality not only enables queries within connected rows but also makes it easier to explore information linked to these rows. For example, entering \'Canada\' will retrieve all users from Canada, even if the reference in the underlying table is only by \'country_id\'.\n- *Multilingual Display & Search* Moreover, the editor displays the translated value if a table cell contains a translation key, improving data readability and comprehension. This feature also extends to the search function, facilitating queries in translated fields if they contain a translation key.\n - *Access Control* The component adheres to the access restrictions set in Access Control.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5178,'resource_documentation_db_fetchall','en','The webservice allows JavaScript to get data from database tables (if the access rights have been set). Instead of giving access to an entire table, it is possible to set (in the Metayota editor under the access), that JavaScript may only access the rows with the user_id having the same value like the logged in user. \n\nYou can call this (like all other webservices), like this:\nGlobalResource.call(\'db.fetchall\', {table: \'recipes\'})',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5179,'resource_documentation_db_get','en','Get a single row from a database with JavaScript (set the corresponding access rights in Access Control). \n\nGlobalResource.call(\'db.get\', {table:\'users\',where:{\'status\':\'active}})',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5180,'resource_documentation_db_row_editor','en','Edit a certain dataset in a database table.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5181,'resource_documentation_db_table','en','Lists all or a selection of rows from a database table.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5182,'resource_documentation_decimal_separator','en','A decimal separator is a dot (.), comma (,), or other symbols that divide a number into whole and fractional parts. Like in 12.34 or 12,34. In $3.50, the dot (.) is the decimal separator which means you have 3 dollars and 50 cents.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5183,'resource_documentation_design_resparameter','en','Internal: Used by the form-generator (form.resource).',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5185,'resource_documentation_dialog','en','Combines a form generator and a modal dialog! Just name the resource type you want to generate the form for and the value! ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5186,'resource_documentation_div','en','Basic container element without styling.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5187,'resource_documentation_document_number_template','en','For example BILL-{year}-####',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5188,'resource_documentation_documentation','en','A description about the resource. What is the purpose of the resource?',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5189,'resource_documentation_dropdown','en','The dropdown form element allows the user to select on or more options from a list. It could be used for example to select a country from a country list. Or any other possible lists.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5191,'resource_documentation_form_array','en','List all types of resources. It uses the form view components to display the various types of data. For example, numbers are formatted with the localized thousands separator and decimal separator, etc.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5192,'resource_documentation_form_button','en','The button form element fires a click event when the button is clicked!',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5193,'resource_documentation_form_checkbox','en','The checkbox offers a yes / no choice.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5194,'resource_documentation_form_date','en','Choose a date from a calendar.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5195,'resource_documentation_form_element','en','Form element',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5196,'resource_documentation_form_file','en',' - File upload form component\n - Set a folder where the file should be uploaded to\n - Define which usergroups are allowed to upload to which folders',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5197,'resource_documentation_form_file_helper','en','It is used by the form.file form element and not meant to be used directly. The form file helper is a tool to display the upload file dialog and to upload the file! The uploader checks if the extension of the file is secure like .jpg or .png, while insecure files like ending with .php could not be uploaded.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5198,'resource_documentation_form_login','en','Authenticate with username and password to the server.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5199,'resource_documentation_form_number','en','An advanced component for facilitating number inputs with enhanced multilingual support and customizable functionalities.\n\n- *Numeric Input*: Enable effortless entry of numbers, adapting to various user needs and preferences.\n- *Suffix Addition*: Allows users to append a suffix to the entered numbers, automatically adjusting to singular, dual, or plural forms to enhance clarity and context.\n- *Multilanguage Support*: Offers a global user experience with full multilingual support, inclusive of language-sensitive suffix adjustments in singular, dual, and plural forms.\n- *Customizable Thousand Separator*: Tailor the thousand group separator to match language preferences, creating a localized and intuitive user interface across different regions.\n- *Language-Dependent Integer Separator*: Adapt the integer separator dynamically based on the selected language, promoting a uniform and localized user interface.\n- *Adjustable Minimum and Maximum Limits*: Define the bounds for input values by setting minimum and maximum limits, helping in error prevention and data consistency maintenance.\n- *Configurable Decimal Precision*: Determine the number of decimals to be displayed, allowing for accurate input representation and customization as per specific needs.\n\nFor detailed guidance and illustrative examples, refer to our comprehensive documentation:\n<a href=\"/form.number.documentation\">Documentation with Examples</a>',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5200,'resource_documentation_form_options_dbrow','en','It displays a dropdown with all rows from a database table. Define which column should be used for the dropdown item text and which for the value. It supports multiselect, translation, etc..',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5201,'resource_documentation_form_password','en','A password field.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5202,'resource_documentation_form_radio','en','Displays radio buttons, comparable to &lt&input type=\"radio\"/&gt;.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5203,'resource_documentation_form_resource','en','If you create a custom action for a step, you can display a form there. This enables attaching a custom form definition to the meeting type; for example, if the meeting type is an online meeting, the custom form could include a text field with a link.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5204,'resource_documentation_form_text','en','The form text element displays a editable text.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5205,'resource_documentation_form_text_translated','en','It is comparable to a form.text, but it is used for multilanguage texts. It displays an input for every language (depending on which languages you have defined the language table). It also has the option to automatically translate the entered value into all other languages.\n\nIt uses all defined languages to make the additonal translations. For example: If you have \"Save\" in English, \"Speichern\" in German, it would translate this to \"Enregistrer\" in French. Because \"Save\" could also be used for \"Saving Money\", but having the translation in another language ensures that the translation is correct. ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5206,'resource_documentation_form_textarea','en','The textarea is a form element for editing a multiline text. ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5207,'resource_documentation_format_text','en','Simple component that converts simple text like lists into HTML.\n\ne.g. \n &ndash; Bullet point 1\n &ndash; Bullet point 2\n\nIs converted into a bullet-point list, &ast; This is a Title &ast; is converted into a *bold text*.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5208,'resource_documentation_framework','en','The Metayota HTML engine is the basic framework code that is used to run your web application and load the tags! Please do not edit this code!',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5209,'resource_documentation_google_sign_in','en','This component displays a \"Sign in with Google\"-Button, so the user has the option to register and login with his Google account, instead of using a username and password combination.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5210,'resource_documentation_group_separator','en','A group separator, like a comma (,) or a dot (.), helps to organize big numbers into easier-to-read groups, usually of three digits. For example, the number 1,000 or 1.000 means one thousand. It separates thousands from hundreds, making it quicker to read and understand the value. Different places use different symbols as group separators.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5211,'resource_documentation_group_separator_characters_count','en','The group separator character count indicates how many digits are grouped together before a separator is used. The most common grouping is by thousands (3 characters), but some regions or systems allow for customization, such as grouping by ten thousand (4 characters). Three characters grouping (1,000 or 1.000): This is widely used globally. Four characters grouping (10,000 or 10.000): This is less common but can be found in certain East Asian countries.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5212,'resource_documentation_image_resize','en','Resize an image with imagemagick. With various options (like crop, mask, format, etc.). It caches the result.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5213,'resource_documentation_index','en','This is the index page for your website. It contains the basic information about your website like the title, the description, keywords for search engines, etc. It is the basis used by the browser in the preinstalled template on your first web app! ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5214,'resource_documentation_innerhtml','en','Allows you to dynamically include HTML content.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5215,'resource_documentation_link','en','The link can contain variables from the SQL result, most likely you will need to use {contact_id}.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5216,'resource_documentation_loader','en','Shows progress.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5217,'resource_documentation_login_problems','en','This page is displayed when the user can no longer login to your website, because he forgot his password or he did not activate his email address. It displays the links to reset his password or resend the mail address verification mail.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5218,'resource_documentation_mail_sender','en','A simple component to send an email. It uses the mail service from the webserver and does not need any authentication!',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5219,'resource_documentation_max_decimal_places','en','Allows the user the enter more decimal places, but still rounds to the \"Decimal Places\" setting if the number doesn\'t require this precision.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5220,'resource_documentation_meeting_form','en','This form will be used when the meeting invitation is sent! (Optional)',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5221,'resource_documentation_meta_description','en','Write in 3-5 sentences what this app is about!',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5222,'resource_documentation_meta_keywords','en','Comma separated list of keywords for search engines',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5223,'resource_documentation_meta_title','en','This Title Is Displayed When Sharing a Website on Social Networks Such as Facebook or X',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5224,'resource_documentation_metayota','en','This is the Metayota PHP engine! With just a few lines of code, it handles everything necessary for your application.\n\n- Access Control (Checks if the user has access rights to the script)\n- Database Functions (like $db->getById(), etc.)\n- Editor integration (Writing the scripts to your webspace)\n- Caching\n- Resource Handling (Packs your tags into a JSON array)\n- Configuration Management (Offers the getConfig()-Function)',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5225,'resource_documentation_namevalue','en','A name value pair (e.g. used for option list with key-value).',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5226,'resource_documentation_options','en','The options are filled with an array (several elements). A JSON object should look like this [{name: \"display name\",value: \"value\"}]. This value is then also emitted at the change event as an event object!',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5227,'resource_documentation_other_id_column','en','In the MySQL table (reference_table) the column that refers to the ID of the selected rows (selected in the dropdown).',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5228,'resource_documentation_paragraph','en','Draws text.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5229,'resource_documentation_parametertype','en','Parameters are used by all types of components (like tags, database-tables, web-services, etc). \n\nFor a tag a parameter is comparable to an HTML attribute <form.number decimal_places=\"2\"></form.number>\nFor a database table, a parameter is comparable to a column.\nFor web-services, it is the definition of what $_POST values a web-service would expect. \n\nSo the parameter types define what parameters are possible (like checkbox, text, long text, etc.). It maps these types to form fields, viewers, MySQL column types, etc.\n\nSo it defines for example that a \"Boolean (Yes/No)\" is edited with a form.checkbox, viewed by view.bool, has the SQL type SMALLINT(1), etc.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5230,'resource_documentation_pii4m5mz','en','Allows to have a custom email template for this meeting type, e.g. to show the custom form parameters, like additoinal information like a link for an online meeting, or if the meeting is physical like a location, etc.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5231,'resource_documentation_rc_icon','en','Basic icons needed by various components (like the database table editor).',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5232,'resource_documentation_rc_registration','en','This is the default registration. You can change the texts in the Implementation-view or add new fields for the form-generator in the Parameters-section. When you introduce new fields, don\'t forget to add them in the database (phpMyAdmin tool, you can login in the \"Your servers\" page)',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5233,'resource_documentation_rc_sync','en','Used by the Metayota editor to synchronize resources to your webspace. Do not delete, if you want to use the \"Update ...\" function, to get the updates of the components.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5234,'resource_documentation_rc_validator_regex','en','A regular expression to validate a form field.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5235,'resource_documentation_rc_view_resource_with_parameters','en','null',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5236,'resource_documentation_reference_table','en','Each row in this table contains a reference to table A and B, and connects them with a many-to-many relationsship.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5237,'resource_documentation_reset_password','en','This is the page where the can reset his password. The link to this page is mailed by the forgot-password component, with a security hash to ensure that it\'s the correct user.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5238,'resource_documentation_resource','en','A resource can be anything: \r\n - Functions\r\n - Tags\r\n - Classes\r\n - Images\r\n - Services\r\n - Object\r\n - Database Table (Object)',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5239,'resource_documentation_resource_name','en','The form generator will display a form with all the parameters of the given resource, and uses the according form elements also defined in the parameters.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5240,'resource_documentation_router','en','The router checks the URL and redirects the user.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5241,'resource_documentation_sql_query','en','When it returns a dataset, the step is considered fulfilled. You can use variables like {contact_id}, or {customer_id} for registerd customers.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5242,'resource_documentation_step_type_template_params','en','JSON with parameter values',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5243,'resource_documentation_success_sql','en','Returns a record if the action was successful. If no record comes back, the action is assumed to have not been executed yet!',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5244,'resource_documentation_tabs','en','The tabs component allows you to switch pages.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5245,'resource_documentation_template_variables','en','JSON containing all possible template variables.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5246,'resource_documentation_title','en','What Is the Text About?',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5247,'resource_documentation_translation_service','en','This PHP-Library allows you to use the translate() function, to translate keys to the current language.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5248,'resource_documentation_translator','en','The translator allows you to add, edit and compare translations. ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5249,'resource_documentation_user','en','The default user database table, that saves all the registered users. Contains columns like first name, last name, mail address, country, password hash, etc.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5250,'resource_documentation_user_obj','en','Here are all the essential information about the current user saved. ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5251,'resource_documentation_validator_javascript','en','Use a custom JavaScript to check your form field is correct. Of course it is also possible to implement your own form field validators in JavaScript!',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5252,'resource_documentation_validator_mail','en','A validator for form fields that check if the entered value is a valid email address like user@domain.com',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5253,'resource_documentation_verify_mail','en','The user gets a link to this page to verify his email address after registration or changing his email.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5254,'resource_documentation_view_array','en','It is the viewer component for the form.array form element. ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5255,'resource_documentation_view_bool','en','This is the view component for form.checkbox! It is used by the database editor and form generator.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5256,'resource_documentation_view_date','en','Readonly form component: Displays the given date in the users preferred date format.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5257,'resource_documentation_view_file','en','Every form component has a corresponding component to display it (e.g. for the database editor, form generator).\n\nThe form component form.file allows you to upload a file, while the view.file displays this file again. When it is a picture, it will display a preview of this picture. ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5258,'resource_documentation_view_link','en','With [id] variable for the row id',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5259,'resource_documentation_view_number','en','This readonly form component displays a number. You can set the decimal-separator, number of decimal places, etc. It is the viewer for form.number.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5260,'resource_documentation_view_options','en','Form component to display a readonly version of the dropdown or form.radio.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5261,'resource_documentation_view_translated_text','en','Every form component like has a corresponding component to view the value (without the ability to edit it). For example form.text has the view component view.text. This is the view component for form.translated.text. It displays the text in the current language.\n\nInternal component: \n - Used by the form generator (form.resource) to display readonly values, when the type is \"translated text\"\n - Used by the database editor (database.table.editor) to display values ',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5262,'resource_documentation_website_contact','en','Contact Us',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5263,'resource_documentation_website_routes','en','The definitions for the URL\'s for your website.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5264,'resource_documentation_website_thankyou','en','\"Thank you for your registration\"-page.',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00:55',1),(5265,'resource_documentation_website_view','en','Tag to display the current page (defined by the router).',NULL,NULL,0,0,'2025-09-05 05:00: